=== Two distinct routes — which strata do they touch? ===

ROUTE A (per-fiber elliptic-Chabauty / Silverman, the EXCEPTIONAL-SET-CLOSURE doc):
  Family E_PCP(q): y^2=x(x+1)(x+q^2), q=a/b parametrized by the Pythagorean-type
  data; the rank-jump locus R={w=-1} stratified by sigma into the Z[sqrt2]-norm-form
  square loci F5=d k^2, F6=d k^2 (d squarefree) + 2-adic v2(b) layers.
  Closure is FIBER BY FIBER: each fiber is a rank-<=1 elliptic curve, Silverman/
  Ingram-Mahe primitive-divisor kills Face-3 squares.  INFINITELY MANY curves
  (one E_PCP per q), each needs its own (finite) N0.  d>1/F5/2-adic = the strata of
  this infinite family.  Per-stratum uniform structure (tor=8, rank-1-in-R) verified,
  but NO single uniform N0 over the infinite family.

ROUTE B (the genus-3 Coleman cover, THIS document):
  ONE fixed curve C': T^2=f(t), t=p/q (Pythagorean parameter of the EULER BRICK).
  C'(Q) <-> ALL PCPs in Saunderson form (full cover, all bricks, all d, all sigma).
  rank J(C')=2 < genus 3 => Coleman gives |C'(Q)| <= 12 in ONE shot, UNCONDITIONAL,
  SIGMA-FREE, and INDEPENDENT of the d/F5/2-adic stratification entirely.

=== The relationship between the two parametrizations ===
Route A's q (the E_PCP modulus, = (m^2-n^2)/(2mn) type) and Route B's t=p/q
(the Euler-brick Pythagorean ratio) are DIFFERENT variables on DIFFERENT moduli.
Route B does not stratify by d at all: the single curve C' subsumes every d,
every F5/F6 value, every 2-adic layer, because the Szpiro ratio sigma never enters.

=== So for step 4 the honest answer is: ===
Route B (genus-3) does NOT need to 'extend' to d>1/F5/2-adic with more curves --
it already covers them ALL with the SINGLE curve C'.  The d-stratification is a
Route-A artifact.  C' is uniform across all of it by construction.

=== The genuine residual gap of Route B (honest) ===
Coleman gives |C'(Q)| <= 12 but proves only FINITENESS+BOUND, not that the 8 known
points are ALL of C'(Q).  Closing 12 -> 8 (ruling out up to 4 hypothetical extra
points, which COULD be non-degenerate PCPs) needs Coleman p-adic integration to
PIN the points = MAGMA (Coleman/QCMod).  PARI gives the bound, not the pinning.
